> **Key Findings:**
> 
> - **Air Pollution Trends and Sources**: Globally, PM2.5 concentrations exceed WHO guidelines, predominantly due to anthropogenic sources. Elevated PM2.5 levels are especially prevalent in densely populated regions like South and East Asia, where the impacts on health are most severe. While some regions may see improvements due to existing policies, others, particularly South Asia, Africa, and Latin America, face rising trends due to industrial and economic activities.
> 
